  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-amazon">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Amazon</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2020–Present · Senior Product Manager, Energy &amp; Sustainability (Jan 2025–Present)<br />Product Manager, Finance (New Product Innovation) (Oct 2022–Jan 2025)<br />Senior Product Analyst, Finance (June 2020–Oct 2022)</p>
    <ul>
      <li>28 of 28 fact sheets cleared legal, PR, and GTM review with zero corrections in 2026. Built and run the AI pipeline behind them with one engineer. Code computes every number from assured data, and a QA gate blocks anything that fails a check.</li>
      <li>Cut production time 51% and the budget by over 90%, removing the need for a $110K-a-year design contract and seasonal temps. Built it for 14 marketplaces and 32 locales, then launched in US English and Spanish first to prove quality.</li>
      <li>Wrote the business case, requirements, and roadmap for the AI platform and its follow-on products, grounded in customer and field input, and won VP and SVP support for the plan.</li>
      <li>Gave Amazon Leo's sales team a sustainability story for enterprise and government buyers who often require one, used in closed-door negotiations and at AWS re:Invent. Built the same for eero's carrier customers.</li>
      <li>Shaped $1B+ in new-business investment decisions across 5 product lines and 15+ businesses, from indoor farming to EV charging to home energy hardware. Made go/no-go calls with no playbook, and two reached CEO-level review.</li>
      <li>My revenue-share structure was adopted in a $300MM+ co-development deal. Owned the business model and cost structure, and re-ran the numbers through several rounds of redlines.</li>
      <li>Finance and GTM partner to Build It, a ~20-person, CEO-sponsored team testing how lean a hardware team can be and still ship. Built the business and demand models, and the team shipped 3 consumer-electronics products.</li>
      <li>Saved $25MM+ in import duties by moving final assembly from China to Vietnam ahead of regulatory change, a first for a new-device program at Amazon. Came in with no operations background.</li>
    </ul>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-heineken">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Heineken USA</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2018–2020 · Senior Strategy Manager, Revenue Management</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Grew organic sales ~$30MM reporting to the CFO, by reworking pricing and promotions for Heineken, Dos Equis, and Tecate with distributors nationwide.</li>
      <li>Built Heineken USA's Revenue Management team from scratch, setting its KPIs and operating rhythm with global leadership.</li>
      <li>Replaced manual reporting with Python and Power BI automation that built sales decks for the commercial teams.</li>
    </ul>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-american-university">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>American University</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">Kogod School of Business · Education</p>
    <ul>
      <li>MBA, concentration in Data Analytics.</li>
    </ul>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-henkel">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Henkel</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2015–2018 · Associate Manager, Revenue Management</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Built the store-level model behind 300%+ Walmart revenue growth on Dial's $0.93 everyday low price. Defended it when Walmart's buyer pushed back on shipment volumes, won agreement, and the launch earned 7 endcaps for the year.</li>
      <li>Drove $55MM in profit across key retail accounts with assortment, pricing, and promotion plans built on price-elasticity models.</li>
      <li>Built Henkel Canada's Revenue Management function from scratch with the Canadian GM and Marketing VP.</li>
    </ul>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-advantage">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Advantage Sales &amp; Marketing</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">2014–2015 · Category Analyst → Category Manager</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ran weekly reporting and Walmart and Sam's Club pitch decks for about 15 CPG clients at once, aimed at growing their distribution.</li>
      <li>Promoted to embedded analytics partner for Sargento and Church &amp; Dwight, turning store-level data into the recommendations they took to Walmart and Sam's Club buyers.</li>
    </ul>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="company-modal" id="modal-arkansas-tech">
    <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Arkansas Tech University</h3>
    <p class="modal-sub">Education</p>
    <ul>
      <li>B.S. in Business Administration, concentration in Management &amp; Marketing.</li>
    </ul>
